sentences.l:
But if of someone having uttered-a-sound or having spoken he had heard,
he would have smashed together of us the heads and the ship’s timbers
with a jagged rock, having thrown;

There was here a certain seer, a man good and great,
Telemus, son of Eurymus, who in seercraft excelled
and, prophesying, grew old among the Cyclopes;

When early-born appeared, rose-fingered Dawn,
then indeed I, my companions having urged on, ordered
themselves to embark and to loose the stern-cables;
